# EvidenceVault API — manual requests.
# Needs the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client) in VS Code.
# Click "Send Request" above any request. Run "login" first: the others reuse its token.

@base = http://localhost:4000/api
@password = EvidenceVault#2026

### Health check (no sign-in)
GET {{base}}/health

### Sign in as the investigator
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "investigator@evidencevault.local",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Who am I? (uses the token from "login")
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### List my cases
GET {{base}}/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Create a case
POST {{base}}/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "caseNumber": "RIB-2026-0002",
  "title": "Test case from requests.http"
}

### Register evidence (uploads README.md as a sample file into case 1)
POST {{base}}/evidence
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=EVBOUNDARY

--EVBOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="caseId"

1
--EVBOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Sample document
--EVBOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="collectedBy"

Det. Demo
--EVBOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="README.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ./README.md
--EVBOUNDARY--

### List evidence (q searches code, title, case number or hash prefix)
GET {{base}}/evidence?q=EV-
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Verify evidence 1
POST {{base}}/evidence/1/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Download evidence 1 (blocked with 409 if the check fails)
GET {{base}}/evidence/1/download
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Wrong password (send this 5 times to see the account lock with 423)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "investigator2@evidencevault.local",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Sign in as the administrator
# @name admin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@evidencevault.local",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### List users (administrator only); shows who is locked
GET {{base}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.token}}

### Unlock investigator2 (check its id in the list above; seeded id is 3)
PATCH {{base}}/users/3
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "unlock": true
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Phase 3: custody, audit, alerts, reports
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Sign in as the custodian
# @name custodian
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "custodian@evidencevault.local",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Sign in as the auditor
# @name auditor
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "auditor@evidencevault.local",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Find the custodian's user id (for toUserId below)
GET {{base}}/users/directory?role=custodian
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Investigator requests a transfer of evidence 1 to the custodian (seeded custodian id is 4)
# @name transfer
POST {{base}}/evidence/1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "toUserId": 4,
  "reason": "Lodging in the evidence room"
}

### Custodian: transfers waiting for me
GET {{base}}/transfers?direction=incoming&status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{custodian.response.body.token}}

### Custodian accepts the transfer
POST {{base}}/transfers/{{transfer.response.body.transfer.id}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{custodian.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "Received in sealed bag"
}

### Full history of evidence 1
GET {{base}}/evidence/1/history
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor.response.body.token}}

### Chain-of-custody report for evidence 1 (fresh integrity check + anchored chain head)
GET {{base}}/evidence/1/report
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor.response.body.token}}

### Audit log, newest first
GET {{base}}/audit?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor.response.body.token}}

### Verify the audit chain (run `npm run tamper:log` first to see it break)
POST {{base}}/audit/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor.response.body.token}}

### Open alerts
GET {{base}}/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor.response.body.token}}

### Acknowledge alert 1 (administrator only)
POST {{base}}/alerts/1/acknowledge
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.token}}

### Dashboard (try it with each token)
GET {{base}}/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{custodian.response.body.token}}
